{"id":"VHH__display__fresnel_viz","collection":"VHH","category":"display","source_path":"VHH/display/fresnel_viz.json","root_names":["VHH::Visualize::Display::fresnel_viz"],"counts":{"nodes":20,"connections":33,"values":17,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Applies a fresnel effect to the vertex color. The fresnel effect changes the colour of the vertex based on the incident angle to the camera. Requires a camera world matrix input. Big thanks to [Ronja's tutorials.](https://www.ronja-tutorials.com/post/012-fresnel/)","documentation_search":"fresnel viz Applies a fresnel effect to the vertex color. The fresnel effect changes the colour of the vertex based on the incident angle to the camera. Requires a camera world matrix input. Big thanks to [Ronja's tutorials.](https://www.ronja-tutorials.com/post/012-fresnel/) Input geo input The geometry to visualize. camera world matrix The selected camera's world matrix. enable On/off switch. If this is off, the object is passed through untouched. edge color The colour at a grazing angle to the camera. center color The colour at a direct angle to the camera. adjust fresnel An fCurve used to modulate the transition from grazing to direct angles.. transparency How transparent the geo display is. 0 = Opaque, 1 = transparent. Output geo output The object.","port_names":["adjust_fresnel","camera_world_matrix","center_color","edge_color","enable","geo_input","geo_output","transparency"],"node_types_search":["Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3","Core::FCurve::evaluate_fcurve","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Graph::terminal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::clamp","Core::Math::dot","Core::Math::matrix_to_SRT","Core::Math::normalize","Core::Math::subtract","Geometry::Properties::get_point_normal","Geometry::Properties::get_point_position","Geometry::Properties::set_geo_property","Rendering::Materials::assign_material","Rendering::Materials::constant_surface_mat","Rendering::Materials::set_geo_property_reference","Unknown","User::Compoun